{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request","id":1556668,"title":"M20 First character - Critique request","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-15T14:55:10-08:00","id":1556668,"title":"M20 First character - Critique request","content":"Hello everyone. I\u2019m a beginner to Mage and i\u2019m hoping to start looking for a group to play with, but before that, I wanted to make a solid character I can take into games. So below is my first attempt at making a Mage: The Ascension (M20) character. I\u2019d love it if you guys could offer feedback, and point out if i\u2019ve forgotten anything or gotten anything wrong. I\u2019m a bit of an introvert, so I tried making a character who\u2019s extremely extroverted, since it would make for an interesting change of pace and should help me build my roleplaying skills.<br /> <br /> While I know he isn\u2019t 100% rule legal according to the M20 sourcebook, I am hoping to make an argument for thematic integrity to the ST.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your feedback.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Name: Magnus Reinher AKA \u201cMagnus the Magnificent\u201d<br /> <br /> Player: (That\u2019d be me)<br /> Chronicle: I hope<br /> <br /> Nature: Sensualist<br /> Demeanor: Rogue<br /> Essence: Dynamic<br /> <br /> Affiliation: None<br /> Sect: None<br /> Concept: Ecstatic Adversary<br /> <br /> <br /> Appearance: A picture is worth a 1000 words, so I had the GPT-Toaster cook me up some pictures:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"151\" height=\"227\" data-align=\"left\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1556671\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1556671\" data-thumb-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1556671&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_left js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img width=\"148\" height=\"222\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1556672\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1556672\" data-thumb-url=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?photoid=1556672&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Height: 205 cm<br /> Weight: 140 Kg<br /> Bodyfat %: Hah, no.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personality: Magnus is a man who NEEDS challenge the way regular people need food and drink. He is a man who is always looking for the next opponent, the next obstacle, the next goalpost, and his medium of choice: Physical competition, especially combat. Magnus is not an agonophile, but he CRAVES adversity. Every blow struck against him is a gift, every Defeat an inspiration. Battle is his love, and a worthy opponent is his lover. Magnus is always in motion, always seeking a new obstacle to overcome, or training to overcome the one he has found. His self-improvement is almost pathological, and he seeks to forever expand his limits.<br /> <br /> But magnus does not seek strength for the sake of domination or self-glorification. He wants to enjoy life, and his body is the tool through which he does it. Thus, to seek greater challenges, he must ever make himself greater as a means. Nor does he bully the weak, or wield his strength solely for selfish reasons. Magnus is aggressively friendly, and will gladly employ his might to help his friends or protect the innocent. Magnus does not see enemies, merely adversaries, and he is actively bored by politics and intrigue. While he is not stupid, he is a man of very specific focus, and he will move as his heart dictates, with little consideration of the greater picture.<br /> <br /> <br /> Backstory (Simplified):<br /> <br /> Magnus Reinher ihas always been a man with a big heart and a big appetite for life. Already large as a kid, Magnus enjoyed brawling with bullies as much as he did playing sports with his friends. Throughout his childhood and adolescent life, Magnus threw himself into every kind of physical sports and disciplines he could, yet despite excelling in many, he always seemed to soon lose interest. However, in his late teens, Magnus found something that struck a true, instinctual cord with him: Pro wrestling. He obsessed over the WWF and WCW, working ceaselessly in his free time to copy and learn the moves of his favorite stars, determined to one day join the circuit himself.<br /> <br /> In his early twenties, he finally got his chance, and after being scouted to a minor league, Magnus was ecstatic to start his new career and chase his dream. It didn't last long. When Magnus learned that wrestling was essentially scripted, combat stunt-choreography, he was devastated, and quit immediately.<br /> <br /> But Magnus has never been a person that lets setbacks slow him down. If Wrestling wasn't real, he would MAKE it real. Magnus began attending street fights in the rough part of town, looking to get into underground fighting rings and test his might against new opponents, using his own improvised style of combat pro-wrestling under the wrestling name he never got to use: &quot;The Magnificent&quot;<br /> <br /> Magnus\u2019 awakening came when he decided to attempt an extreme weightlifting challenge by bench-pressing the back end of a car. The jack he was using as a safety slipped, and while Magnus should have been crushed, he poured every ounce of his strength and willpower into lifting the car off of himself, triggering his awakening. The surge of life magic that coursed through him as he saw the vision of his avatar allowed him to empower his muscles and save himself, and set him on his path of greater challenges as a mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ATTRIBUTES<br /> <br /> <br /> Physical (Primary)<br /> <br /> Strength: 5 (1 point bought for 5 freebies)<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 4<br /> Specialties: Strength \u2013 Overpower, Stamina \u2013 Tireless<br /> <br /> Notes: Magnus is meant to be a physical powerhouse. An absolute brick of a man. He is an accomplished athlete, and while he is not clumsy, strength and fortitude are his primary focus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mental (Secondary)<br /> <br /> Perception: 3<br /> Intelligence: 2<br /> Wits: 3<br /> <br /> Notes: Magnus is attentive and able to make quick judgements (when his interest is engaged) and while he is by no means a genius, neither is he a fool.<br /> <br /> <br /> Social (Tertiary)<br /> Charisma: 2<br /> Manipulation: 1<br /> Appearance: 3<br /> <br /> Notes: Magnus is absolutely guileless. While he is smart enough that he could attempt to manipulate people, he has absolutely zero interest in doing so. While he is not conventionally handsome, his physical presence is imposing, and his natural warmth and enthusiasm lends him a certain charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> ABILITIES<br /> <br /> <br /> Talents (Primary)<br /> <br /> Brawl: 5<br /> Athletics: 4<br /> Expression: 2<br /> Alertnesss: 1<br /> Awareness: 1<br /> <br /> Specialties: Brawl \u2013 Power move, Athletics \u2013 Bodybuilding<br /> <br /> Notes: Magnus is using pro-wrestling as an actual combat style (Think King from Tekken 8) and is a consumate bodybuilder. Expression is meant to signify his showmanship as a wrestler. While Magnus isn\u2019t inattentive, he usually doesn\u2019t care enough to pay that much attention, hence low awareness and alertness. I am aware that these stats are over the 3 point starter limit, but given his specialization and theme, I am hoping ST would approve.<br /> <br /> <br /> Skills (Secondary<br /> <br /> Meditation: 3<br /> Research: 2<br /> Survival: 2<br /> <br /> Notes: Meditation is meant to be a measure of Magnus\u2019 ability to \u201cget in the zone\u201d more than any cerebral discipline. Magnus is mostly autodidact, which is the purpose of his research skill, and he likes going camping. I know I didn\u2019t use all the points available here, but adding more skill points, or different skills, didn\u2019t feel like they fit his theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> Knowledges (Tertiary)<br /> Medicine: 2<br /> Esoterica: 2<br /> Occult: 1<br /> <br /> Medicine is for his knowledge of nutrition and supplements, knowing which stimulants are safe or harmful, and any chemical enhancements (Magnus does NOT use steroids. This is meant for peak HEALTH not short-term gain) Esoterica is for his knowledge of natural suplements, folk medicine, etc. Occult is due to his interest in supernatural training methods and suplements after awakening as a mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> SPHERES<br /> <br /> <br /> Life (Affinity): 3<br /> Forces: 2<br /> Matter: 1<br /> <br /> Note: Magnus\u2019 style of magic is meant to be focused around two core concepts: Long term ritual Life magic to incrementally enhance and rebuild his body beyond human limits, and short term power boosts via Life and forces for combat performance. Essentially he is using life magic for supernatural bodybuilding to turn himself naturally superhuman, while also using it to boost his performance in critical situations when necessary.<br /> <br /> He is meant to be paradox light, disguising most of his magic behind wrestling theatrics, and making life magic effects look like stunt choreography, adrenaline spikes or extremele physical effort for someone who\u2019s already absolutely massive. he prefers not to use magic unless he runs into a threat he can\u2019t overpower naturally, after all there\u2019s no fun in just beating an opponent down in an unfair fight. Magnus understands that paradox is a thing, and will save overtly impossible feats for fighting supernatural threats.<br /> <br /> <br /> ADVANTAGES<br /> <br /> <br /> Arete: 3 (2 points bought for 8 freebies)<br /> Willpower: 9 (+4 points bought for 4 freebies)<br /> <br /> Note: Magnus is meant to be a naturally powerful mage in tune with himself, but without any formal training. His style of magic is very instinctual and intuitive.<br /> <br /> <br /> Resources: 2<br /> Fame: 1<br /> Contacts: 1<br /> Node: 1<br /> Avatar: 2<br /> <br /> Note: I gave him resources 2 because Magnus lifestyle requires him to have things like gym equipment, supplements, and food (A LOT of food) and he should be making some money off of his underground fights.<br /> Fame is for the same reason, he\u2019s basically a known quantity in the underground fight scene. Maybe a few old promo posters from his Pro wrestling debut, that kind of thing.<br /> Contacts is his fight promoter in the underground, essentially his \u201cagent\u201d who gets him fights.<br /> <br /> His Node is a spot he found in an overgrown corner of an old run down park that he uses as his favorite training spot, because it just \u201cfelt right\u201d and he had an easier time getting in the \u201czone\u201d when he trains there.<br /> Avatar is to signify that while the Avatar is an important presence in Magnus\u2019 life, it is not the driving force behind his lifestyle.<br /> <br /> <br /> MERITS AND FLAWS<br /> <br /> <br /> Merit: Code of honor (Cost 1 freebie)<br /> Flaw: Driven (+3 Freebies)<br /> <br /> <br /> Note: These seemed appropriate given his personality, even if they aren\u2019t listed in the M20 sourcebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> FOCUS<br /> <br /> <br /> Paradigm: The World Exists to be Experienced<br /> <br /> Practice: Form in Motion<br /> <br /> Instruments:<br /> <br /> Doing reps<br /> Diet and Rest<br /> Flexing<br /> \u201cHype up\u201d slaps<br /> Proclamation<br /> Cutting a promo<br /> Pep talks<br /> <br /> Note: Magnus magic is based around bodybuilding and his pro-wrestling persona. If people are interested I have some Rotes i\u2019ve been working on too that illustrates this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Resonance: Dynamic 3<br /> Resonance flavor: Joyous Challenger (i\u2019m not entirely sure how this works)<br /> <br /> Note: Powerful dynamic resonance seemed fitting given his personality and high starting Arete.<br /> <br /> <br /> Avatar description:<br /> <br /> <br /> Magnus' avatar is a distant, towering shape that radiates power and vigor. To Magnus, it is a distant goal, the final challenge, the promise of a great, climactic battle of his life. The avatar rarely speaks, Magnus senses it more through abstract attentions. When Magnus grows and triumphs, the Avatar watches him with interest. When he fails and falters, it disregards him. Only a worthy rival has significance, and that is what the Avatar is to Magnus: Not a friend, but the promise of an opponent that rivals and matches him intimately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","user":"Ironguard","date":". 12-15-2025, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","name":"Ironguard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T11:43:52-08:00","id":1556727,"title":"","content":"I've liked the idea of the &quot;wrestling wizard&quot; since I saw the movies and cartoons of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Santo\" target=\"_blank\">El Santo</a> , figthing mummies, devils and whatnot. So, best of luck.<br /> <br /> *In my opinion, the Avatar and goals of the character don't suggest a Dynamic Essence. I would suggest Questing as it presents itself as an &quot;imaginary apex&quot; to power a constant quest to find stronger opponents, I could see also Static as a &quot;Tower&quot; it's a powerful symbol of stability and &quot;bodibuilding&quot; can be seen as constructing the perfect body, or Primordial as a primeval force that guides the character's powerful, almost instinctual, desire for life (very Conan-esque). Dynamic suggests ever-shifting creativity, constant change, It would fit better if the Avatar was a sort of moving goalpost more than an apex.<br /> <br /> Maybe you think you <i>need </i>it to be Dynamic for your Ressonance?, but really that's an optional rule unless you're playing Revised. And Joy doesn't need to only be Dynamic.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, Ressonance works &quot;colouring&quot; your magick and your character - it's like a &quot;vive check&quot;, you give those vives. And it changes according on how you use your magick (if the guy gets into a lot of violent conflicts, it's going to become more &quot;violent&quot;. If he kills an opponent with magick, he's going to start giving a more grimm and less joyfull vive).<br /> <br /> *Given his inspiration and goals, &quot;Wrestling&quot; (as in, the figthing style that he loved so much he broke trough the Consensus to make it real) seems like it would make an excelent Instrument - that would allow him to fuse magick and wrestling directly, instead of just &quot;buffing&quot; it, effectively &quot;making wrestling real&quot; - if it isn't on the Practice, remember that you can have more than one Practice (Up to 3, I think).<br /> <br /> *In case you need to be part of the Traditions: With that name and constant desire for challenge and overcomming obstacles, if it wasn't because he hates politics and runs on instinct more than structure, he would make a great Hermetic. Extatic does work better &quot;as is&quot;, as the character seems to fall in love with the <i>experience</i> of strength, the Paradigm seems to fit. An unorthodox Akashic could also work, and be pretty funny. Even if nor a &quot;kung fu guy&quot;, I would guess he likes everyone to &quot;be better&quot; themselves, and train their bodies and minds to break personal barriers - that aligns with the goals of the Tradition even if he doesn't do DO (and, <i>with that attitude</i>, he's likely going to get into a lot of figths against strong figthers there :P).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T18:23:40-08:00","id":1556737,"title":"","content":"To begin with, I like it. For a first ever it's quite good.<br /> <br /> My observations will have a few goals, then: verify if you understood everything, clarifying rules and setting in case you didn't, help you to round up the character concept, and increase your chances of having this character approved for a game.<br /> <br /> 1 - A Mage without affiliation or training is an Orphan. And depending on the chronicle and the ST an Orphan may face a lot of extra problems. You shouldn't make one and not expect to play through the hardships of being marginalized in Mage society. They're also unlikely to know a lot about what they are and how it all works, as they had no formal explaining. Again, it depends on the ST, but you shouldn't expect the Avatar or anyone else to have supplied the character with any information at all about what Magic is, related phenomena and the factions around you.<br /> <br /> So, are you sure this is what you want? By definition this isn't something he'll overcome easily or through Magic or at all. Your concept works just fine within a Tradition, even within the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> 2 - For whatever it's worth, fight is fight, bodybuilding is bodybuilding, weight lifting is weight lifting. They require distinct training regimens, diets, skills and muscles. This distinction is both in terms of description and of what traits in the sheet they justify or need. It's also a social distinction, as there's a lot of contempt between those three groups. Bodybuilding also isn't healthy in any way.<br /> <br /> In game terms, you'll need Dexterity to be a good fighter, as it's still what you'll roll for attacks, and even a wrestler can do with slightly less Strength, especially an Awakened wrestler. I agree that Stamina being high is good for a physical character that's a generalist and a healthy person, but I'd move at least 1 dot from Strength to Dexterity if the main idea is for him to be a good fighter. It also begs the question if your idea really require him to start play already at the absolute peak human form, or if he has still some space for growth before inhuman performance starts to kick in.<br /> <br /> Of course, it may just be a case of clarifying the concept or adapting it a little to reflect the actual dots. A character that primarily seeks fights would be on a more classical fighting mindset, but for a Mage it isn't unsuitable the idea of trying to be everything.<br /> <br /> 3 - IME there are two kinds of STs when it comes to the 3 dots limit on starting Abilities: those who ignore it altogether and those who never do. The first will probably tell you ahead of time that you can have starting Abilities above 3. The second, though, won't be happy to see you already built your character like that without at least a back-up plan in case of a hard &quot;no&quot;, and they'll give you a hard &quot;no&quot;, no discussion.<br /> <br /> So, I'd have a back-up plan. Take another Flaw, move some dots, again rethink if you need the character to have extreme levels of skill right out of the bat. 3 dots is plenty for the concept as it is now, anyway, a fighter with 5-6 dice for attacks and 3-4 Strength is plenty to be a locally successful Sleeper wrestler.<br /> <br /> 4 - King is not a Tekken 8 character. They're Tekken characters, period (two characters wore the mantle, or the mask, of King). King is in every single entry of the franchise.<br /> <br /> 5 - Don't dismiss the value of 1-dot Abilities both as game stats and background elements. The character had a whole life before play begins and not every waking moment was about becoming what they are today. You can use those two dots to put some extra color on him, a bit of trivia, talk about upbringing, anything.<br /> <br /> 6 - Occult isn't just interest on the supernatural, it may be even the simple fact that he's aware of it as, being an Orphan, this isn't a given for him.<br /> <br /> 7 - You must define what is Magic for him, especially he being an Orphan. Magic is a malleable concept within the game, it means different things for different Mages. Does he even thinks about it as anything but an extension of his training?<br /> <br /> Ascension's Mages aren't like D&amp;D Sorcerers. They didn't discovered they have strange powers (well, unless they did). They noticed the world was <i>more</i>, that <b>they</b> could be more, but what it means is extremely personal. For someone like Magnus the notion that the human body and mind simply <b>is</b> capable of doing exceptional feats if you dedicate and learn how to seems like a fitting Paradigm. In this case, it could well be that he doesn't hold back his Magic because he doesn't even understand it as &quot;magic&quot;, but as the simple result of his constant self-improvement.<br /> <br /> Magic is central to a Mage, not just in the sense of being the core powers, but it isn't really magic. It's their worldview, it's drive, it's your destiny, things Magnus already have, but you describe as distinct. Your Avatar in particular doesn't simply exists to help you improve, it exists to help you improve <u>your Magic</u>. It's also how the world works for you, not just in the sense of your opinion, but that Mages literally can't be proven wrong, what they believe they make real in an undeniable, concrete sense, and so it <b>does</b> work like that in an absolute sense. It's the ability to make wondrous things, not because you have &quot;strange powers&quot;, but because you have drive and vision and you know how the world really works, which may or may not be some sort of power.<br /> <br /> It isn't even necessarily the same phenomenon despite using the same rules. The Technocracy stance is that what they do is Science and has nothing really to do with what Mages do, the Order of Hermes defends that everyone is fundamentally doing the same thing and this is formally the official stance of the Traditions, many Mages believe what some groups do is the same as them, but others not, and many believe whatever <i><b>they</b></i> do is absolutely unique to them. And any of them may be right.<br /> <br /> Someone like Magnus would probably be completely out of this discussion, but would still have an opinion about what he does. But what he does, while Magic for game terms and Hermetic theory, isn't necessarily magic at all.<br /> <br /> That's why we always use Magic with uppercase M, and many with the <i>pretentious K</i> in Magick. Pretentious or not, it's a conceptually extremely important distinction in the setting. There are plenty magic users, by the way, who are Sleepers.<br /> <br /> 8 - I'm sure it would be good to see your rotes.<br /> <br /> 9 - How Resonance flavor works is an ST decision with some of the most vague and inconsistent rules through the history of the game, don't sweat it.<br /> <br /> But Resonance <i><b>value</b></i>, not so much, and 3 is <b>A LOT</b>.<br /> <br /> The normal Resonance level for the most ardent normal humans and sites of legend is, still, 0. 1 is possible, but requires some <i>je ne sais quoi</i> to happen.<br /> <br /> At 3 Magnus is already becoming <i><b>overtly</b></i> supernatural just by being there. Not a big thing, but enough for some <i>normal, but perceptive</i> people to notice he is undeniably inhuman. It isn't just a measure of how much he has some personality trait, it's a measure of how much this <i><b>seeps into reality passively</b></i>. It lightly alters the environment, it affects the mood of people around him, and it shapes his Effects, not just methods, regardless of his will.<br /> <br /> I do not recommend arbitrarily increasing Resonance without experience with the game and the ST, it isn't a measure of personality or awesomeness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556727#post1556727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've liked the idea of the &quot;wrestling wizard&quot; since I saw the movies and cartoons of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Santo\" target=\"_blank\">El Santo</a> , figthing mummies, devils and whatnot. So, best of luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had until recently a PC in my current chronicle with a very similar vibe and view on Magic. The difference is that he was an accomplished boxer (using Magic in the ring without noticing it at first, and then not caring anymore because it is what it is, he didn't saw it as cheating). And he was, in fact, an Hermetic from House Tytalus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T23:45:47-08:00","id":1556748,"title":"","content":"I don't have much to add that isn't covered in the two posts above, but I think it's worth stressing a few things:<br /> <br /> First off, how is this character going to work in a game with multiple PCs? This can be a problem for many types of mages, as it's not uncommon for mages to have such a strong drive towards their goals. But what does he do within a group when there's no fighting to do? Being so narrowly focused as a character can make it hard to find a place with other characters to form the basis of a PC group. Whether or not going for an Orphan is what you're after, he's going to struggle to be part of a functional social unit because he's busy chasing the high of his next fight and might not even realize the impact he'd have on people trying to work with him (Empathy/Subterfuge both as 0 means he's not very good at figuring out how people feel, and Streetwise/Etiquette 0 means he's not great at navigating social norms). Pulling back a bit not only would give you more room to grow in his primary focus in-play, but also free up points for him having a bit more capable in other situations.<br /> <br /> Second, a bit beyond considering higher Dexterity and having Life magic to buff Soak and healing, I would not considering this a character that's really ready to survive in the World of Darkness. This applies very much to surviving serious fights (esp. unregulated fights where an opponent that palms a razor could easily mess up another), but also to the broader brutality of the setting. The setting is even more full of liars, cheats, and con artists than our own. It's a world where most people that are ready to use violence to solve their problems aren't going to care about fighting fair or the mutual growth of mutually agreed to fights. The setting is also full of people that will easy tease out how driven he his, and without him knowing it, then point him into dangerous situations while they keep their hands clean. Even taking his promoter as a Contact instead of Allies or a Mentor means his promoter isn't in this for Magnus's well being. From both mechanical and narrative perspectives, this is a character that's going to get chewed up and spat out by the dark nature of the setting.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I would consider that Skills and Knowledges have penalties for being rated at 0. Knowledges in particular have the harshest penalty as you don't get a roll at all if you don't have any dots. Academics or Science 0? Unless your ST considers something such basic knowledge you don't need to roll for it at all, you auto-fail. It's an incredibly risky thing to not even leave your character a chance to make basic checks on things like their legal rights, operating computers, knowing what's in famous works of art, doing math, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T08:07:40-08:00","id":1556752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even taking his promoter as a Contact instead of Allies or a Mentor means his promoter isn't in this for Magnus's well being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about this, since this character it's supposed to be an extrovert, it could help to start from the get-go with a wider and healtier social circle to interact with, rather than focus so much on his personal skills. I imagine most extroverts do relate with, and depend on, other people.<br /> <br /> Like, he's a cheerfull figther, he should have made a few friends on the wrestling scene (the staff, people that go there to sell stuff, maybe friendly rivals) - As Allies and/or Contacts.<br /> <br /> A trainer/Mentor giving him advice could be good, like how Rocky had Mickey Goldmill. The character doesn't need to be a mage, just someone that knows the scene and wants magnus to improve and become a legend ... and that would help the Storyteller to convey what's necessary to survive on their &quot;underground&quot;.<br /> \u200b<br /> And having the Mentor or an Ally to be his promoter it's very good, considering he's the guy that's involved in the politicking and management behind the figths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T00:31:41-08:00","id":1556781,"title":"","content":"I appreciate all the feedback guys, and i'm happy to clarify a few things in response <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ALEPH<br /> <br /> The reason I picked dynamic essence is because the Avatar is meant to be an unreachable goal. What Magnus seeks is challenge, not accomplishment. Self improvement is the vehicle, not the goal. What he\u2019s chasing is the feeling of overcoming his limits, again and again. Fighting and bodybuilding are just the things he enjoy the most, but there\u2019s nothing other than his own choices that limits him to that. I can see the argument for primordial, since Magnus is someone who enjoys life, which is part of his paradigm, but I wanted to illustrate that he is the kind of person that is always in motion, always looking for something to do.<br /> <br /> I did consider adding wrestling as an instrument, it just seemed like it might be too encompassing. I might swap it out for one of the others, and I do have ideas for a few rotes that act like offensive moves (mostly with the use of Forces)<br /> <br /> He does have some overlap with several traditions, I just started him out as an Orphan since I made him from the perspective of a newly awakened mage. If necessary for the story for him to be part of a tradition, adjustments can be made. As you mentioned, Cult of Ecstacy, Akashics and certain hermetic houses could be an option.<br /> <br /> Magnus isn\u2019t an extrovert in the sense that he has a large social circle or particularly adept social skills, its more that he wears his heart on his sleeve, and acts with almost overwhelming affection. Magnus will devote himself fully to people he know in the moment, but he isn\u2019t the kind of person you can tie down with commitment. He\u2019s always in motion, always moving on to the next thing, and if you don\u2019t keep up, he\u2019ll leave you behind or drift away.<br /> <br /> <br /> MONTEPARNAS<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. As mentioned above, this is mostly dependent on the chronicle. He doesn\u2019t need to be an Orphan, it just seemed to fit best as a baseline<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. Not quite sure what you are getting at here. If you\u2019re referring to cosmetic bodybuilding, that\u2019s not what Magnus is doing. He\u2019s using training to build hollistic strength, both to allow himself to fight better and for generally higher performance and health. He\u2019s not training to be a powerlifter if that\u2019s what you mean.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3. Well, worst case, I could move a few dots from brawl and athletics for something else. I mostly wanted them there because it fit thematically.<br /> <br /> 4. I am aware, but Tekken 8 had the best illustration, and I don\u2019t expect people to research the entire Tekken series to know what i\u2019m talking about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> 5. I considered this, but Magnus is meant to be a very singleminded individual. He\u2019ll pursue an interest wholeheartedly, with little interest for anything unrelated, which is why most of his skills are picked to support his fighting and training habits.<br /> <br /> <br /> 6. Well, it works either way I feel. Even if it\u2019s simply instinctual awareness that weird things are real.<br /> <br /> <br /> 7. To Magnus, magick is unbound potential. It is the rejection of absolute limits, the ability to look reality in the eye, and answer \u201cYou are wrong, and I will prove it\u201d when it tells you that something is impossible. That said, Magnus Magick is meant to be more instinctual and emotional and cerebral. He\u2019s not doing math equations or singing holy hymns.<br /> <br /> <br /> 8. These are more rote concepts than fully detailed ones, I still need to read up some more on the rules for spellcasting. They are mainly meant to focus around self-buffing stats, soak and healing, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> 9. I\u2019m not entirely clear on how resonance levels work, I just read that you could give characters up to 3 points to start with, and Magnus is meant to be LOUD, both metaphysically and personally. I don\u2019t have any specific investment here, so I can tune that down.<br /> <br /> <br /> HEAVY ARMS<br /> <br /> Magnus is meant to be\u2026 a character that keeps things moving. Magnus is the kind of guy you want to point at the trouble you want him to get into, because if you don\u2019t, he\u2019s going to get into trouble on his own. I don\u2019t plan to have him just run off at the drop of the hat, but he is meant to help keep the story from stalling into endless discussion, planning and argument. Magnus isn\u2019t stupid (I did give him int 2) but he has a very specific set of priorities, however, he is also meant to be friendly, and care about the people around him, so he\u2019s not going to just endanger them for his own fun.<br /> <br /> As mentioned above, I do plan to use life magic for things like protection (bio-kinetic armor, healing self and others) and stat boosts. I may shift another point to dexterity, it was more meant to show that his fighting style is more about overwhelming power than finesse. As a wrestler he\u2019s focused around grappling, throwing, knocking opponents down, that kind of thing, more than punching and kicking. As for Magnus being susceptible to manipulation: well that\u2019s kind of the point. Magnus doesn\u2019t really CARE if you\u2019re manipulating him, as long as it serves his own interest of finding new opponents. If it doesn\u2019t\u2026 well, to quote mensc: \u201cFool me once, shame on you, fool me twice, watch out, i\u2019m huge!\u201d<br /> <br /> In terms of peripheral knowledge, Magnus simply doesn\u2019t really care that much. Magnus doesn\u2019t have what you would consider a normal modern mindset. He\u2019s more like a questing knight or a wandering warrior in terms of attitude. If he hadn\u2019t become a mage, he would probably have ended up eventually wandering the third world looking for trouble, or getting thrown in prison (he still might, I suppose)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","name":"Ironguard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T02:29:33-08:00","id":1556783,"title":"","content":"So apparently, the system thinks my response post may be spam. If prior experiences is anything to go by, it might take a couple of weeks before it gets approved... Guess i'll get to work compiling my rote concepts in the meantime -_-<br /> <br /> Edit: Guess i was wrong. At least they approve posts faster than accounts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","user":"Ironguard","date":". 12-18-2025, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","name":"Ironguard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T12:44:32-08:00","id":1556806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He\u2019s always in motion, always moving on to the next thing, and if you don\u2019t keep up, he\u2019ll leave you behind or drift away.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, keep in mind that we're taking into account that you're making a character without a group to play with yet. What might make sense for a character broadly is not necessarily what is a good idea for your first character with a new group. A new play group is going to need to see some flexibility from you as a player to adapt to the player dynamics. A lot of people have had bad experiences with people that prioritize &quot;well this is what my character would think/do/want&quot; as if you the player have no say in why that's the case.<br /> <br /> Why does anyone want their characters to be forces to &quot;keep up&quot; with Magnus? Why wouldn't the other mages just let him run off if he has no commitment to making their social organization work? Especially considering that Magnus is committed to the flat out weakest form of combat (unarmed and unarmored) in the WoD system (and yes, he has magic, but so do people that use blades or guns along with armor), it's not like he's actually some highly valuable combat asset that you'd consider putting up with some of his personal quirks to get some heavy hitter options. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He\u2019s using training to build hollistic strength, both to allow himself to fight better and for generally higher performance and health. He\u2019s not training to be a powerlifter if that\u2019s what you mean. </div> </div> </div>I'd drop the comment about body fat from his description (and possibly find a more realistic image). Holistic strength, health, and real combat means you want more body fat than average, not less. While it is true that many athletes aim for the lower end of healthy body fat, combat training is not one of them. Fat is padding that helps you absorb blows so your muscles and bones can last longer in a fight. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magnus is meant to be\u2026 a character that keeps things moving. </div> </div> </div>Unless a ST specifically asks you to make a specific type of character that they think will help with the plot? Don't assume this. The vast majority of the time players don't know what the plot is, and thus have no idea how to keep things moving. It's possible to be helpful with this kind of approach, but it's far more likely that you're just going to be a headache for your ST and other players.<br /> <br /> Mages are at their strongest when they take time to think and plan. Most players are going to want to have time to do that. Most STs are going to plan the game around the idea that the mages are going to at least try to be smart about things. One PC that constantly runs off to do his own thing if stuff &quot;slows down&quot; too much is a disruption, not something helpful.<br /> <br /> You also haven't really answered my question. &quot;But what does he do within a group when there's no fighting to do?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magnus isn\u2019t stupid (I did give him int 2) but he has a very specific set of priorities, however, he is also meant to be friendly, and care about the people around him, so he\u2019s not going to just endanger them for his own fun. </div> </div> </div>It's more fair to say that you've presented a character that will not do this <b>intentionally</b>. Accidentally or via manipulation is a serious consideration. You're handing this PC to a potential ST and they're going to see that Driven Flaw on your sheet. He can be the friendliest guy in the WoD, but more pragmatic characters are going to see him as a tool or a liability depending on the circumstances; not someone worth putting a lot of energy into being real friends with... it's not like he's bound to last long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...it was more meant to show that his fighting style is more about overwhelming power than finesse. </div> </div> </div>While the WoD mechanics are not meant to be realistic, they're not meant for this kinda of expression either. To represent the setting as intended, the mechanics heavily favor characters that fight smart via force multiplication rather than brute strength. Outside of exceptions born of specific supernatural powers (like Potence for vampires) the only way to make a great fighter in the system is to make a balanced fighter. Higher Strength and average Dexterity might be fine for a bar brawl, but it's going to fail against a serious opponent, or just a group of enemies, fast. Even with magic (keeping in mind that casting magic takes time, or you have to put up with the consequences of doing long ritual magic to get high duration effects and have those up a lot which has downsides to consider as well), the system heavily favors offense and range. Even with using magic to let Magnus Soak lethal damage and boost his Stamina a bit, three guys with shotguns and a few rounds before Magnus can close on them is going to lead to a dead Magnus. That's just the reality of the system. Add in skill or magic on the side of the shooters and he'll be lucky to survive before he gets to do anything. Vampires and werewolves can afford to charge into combat and rely on their supernatural durability, mages can't. So mages can't afford to be cavalier about their survival odds; hence my phrasing of it as a matter of survival in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magnus doesn\u2019t really CARE if you\u2019re manipulating him, as long as it serves his own interest of finding new opponents. If it doesn\u2019t\u2026 well, to quote mensc: \u201cFool me once, shame on you, fool me twice, watch out, i\u2019m huge!\u201d </div> </div> </div>I'm not asking Magnus to care. I'm asking you to care about the implications of this for making Magnus work in a group play situation. Magnus is a fictional character of your design. If you tell a potential ST and potential play group that you made a character that doesn't care about significant concerns to both his ability to do the things you want him to do mechanically, or care about how well he actually functions in the group? You're also saying that you, as a player, don't care that much about them. Magnus's lack of caring ultimately is a choice you make.<br /> <br /> And as I've gone into more depth on, being huge isn't really a threat in this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556783#post1556783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently, the system thinks my response post may be spam. If prior experiences is anything to go by, it might take a couple of weeks before it gets approved... Guess i'll get to work compiling my rote concepts in the meantime -_-</div> </div> </div> </div>It rarely takes that long when the auto-spam filter acts up. Just remember that a one of very small number of humans have to poke the forums when it happens, and they have busy lives beyond getting to these things. It can feel like a long time because when we have the most free time to post, they're trying to spend their free time doing fun things too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T13:55:46-08:00","id":1556807,"title":"","content":"Well, i was talking more in terms of long-term relationships and overall personality. He'll stay with the group as long as he's invested in them (which would be as long as the chronicle lasts) Plus he is made to be a young, inexperienced mage, ideally paired with other similar mages. If the chronicle is focused around a cabal who actually know what they're doing, i'd have to adjust him significantly. I really focused far more on making him thematic rather than efficient. I'm not going to start to try to metagame right off the bat, not that that'd be much fun regardless.<br /> <br /> The comment about bodyfat was mostly meant as a joke.<br /> <br /> As for what he does for the group when there's no fighting: Moral support? Lift heavy things if they need it? Healing/Recovery? depends on the situation, there's plenty of creative and useful applications for strength, and he's not a meathead. He can help out with research, he's got some knowledge about anatomy and biochemistry, he has meditation, so he could plausibly help characters with centering themselves and recovering from mental stresses.<br /> <br /> as for the close combat aspect, he IS intended to use life magic to eventually move past the 5 maximum of stats (i am aware that will incur permadox or genetic flaws) i'm aware i can't just bulldoze him through everything, besides, what fun would that be?<br /> <br /> I'm aware that can get him killed. I suspect it probably will, eventually. The fun part is going to be trying to avoid that while staying true to his character as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","name":"Ironguard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T23:37:44-08:00","id":1556824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What he\u2019s chasing is the feeling of overcoming his limits, again and again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember that Dynamic Mages are starters, not necessarily finishers, but I do think, you got it right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did consider adding wrestling as an instrument, it just seemed like it might be too encompassing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. As mentioned above, this is mostly dependent on the chronicle. He doesn\u2019t need to be an Orphan, it just seemed to fit best as a baseline</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's fair, but be aware that some STs may let you go with it and then punish you harshly in-game for being an Orphan, and they won't necessarily let you join a faction during the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Not how I would run it, but interpretations on what being an Orphan means and entails are all over the place.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Not quite sure what you are getting at here. If you\u2019re referring to cosmetic bodybuilding, that\u2019s not what Magnus is doing. He\u2019s using training to build hollistic strength, both to allow himself to fight better and for generally higher performance and health. He\u2019s not training to be a powerlifter if that\u2019s what you mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just that those three things are stricter definitions than most people think, for a lot of reasons. So if you want to <b><i>seriously commit</i></b> to the description of a fighter, you should drop the description of something else. And strictly speaking, I <u><b>am</b></u> nitpicking here, just in the spirit of polishing the description.<br /> <br /> Bodybuilding is cosmetic by definition, even when it doesn't involve steroids. Growing muscle size does not significantly increase muscle strength or resilience, and sometimes may even decrease them, even if done only with specialized nutrition and exercises. Huge muscles <i>look</i> strong. They're not.<br /> <br /> Lifting power in general is the result of exercising a localized and specialized set of muscles. Overall that applies to any superlative feat, but it may be quite significant for lifters. People with high Strength as measured by the system aren't necessarily good at a lot of tasks, much less have a balanced muscle growth. Here the greater problem is the big difference between Strength and Dexterity.<br /> <br /> Fighters are generalists. Give or take small differences due to fighting style, none of them can afford over-developing a muscle group in lieu of others, or as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Heavy Arms</a> said, adequate amounts of fat. A pugilist still needs strong legs, a rikishi (sumo wrestler) needs agility and fast reactions, jujutsu practitioners need precision and hand coordination to get a hold of the opponent, and anyone who can't reliably avoid being hit in the first place will soon be seeing stars (or worse).<br /> <br /> Sure, this doesn't means the character can't be strong or physically impressive, but it does mean he wouldn't be caught dead calling what he does as bodybuilding, and probably doing extreme heavy lifts wouldn't be a common thing as they just harm the muscles for no appreciable gain for fighting purposes.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Well, worst case, I could move a few dots from brawl and athletics for something else. I mostly wanted them there because it fit thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, it's just that you should have this alternative ready. I do personally think this is over-commitment for a starting character, but you do what you will.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 4. I am aware, but Tekken 8 had the best illustration, and I don\u2019t expect people to research the entire Tekken series to know what i\u2019m talking about</div> </div> </div> </div>But this actually requires them to look for a specific entry without knowing the comparative relevance.<br /> <br /> Hit &quot;King Tekken&quot; on google and you're good to go, this will deliver far more relevant results and still include the latest depictions, without a meaningless constraint.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. I considered this, but Magnus is meant to be a very singleminded individual. He\u2019ll pursue an interest wholeheartedly, with little interest for anything unrelated, which is why most of his skills are picked to support his fighting and training habits.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's not the point.<br /> <br /> Where did he come from? Does he have a family? Where did he grew? What was his life like before he could devote all his time to being a wrestler? Not just the part where he practiced sports (which by itself may indicate learning a lot of other things as it wasn't just fighting at first), but didn't he attend school, had chores, live with people?<br /> <br /> It's ok to have a concept where the character is single-minded and only cares about one thing. But the point of the setting is, especially as it pertains to the rules for Starting Abilities, that this isn't really something that exists in the world, because your character did not grew up in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> Not everything we know is our calling in life, even for those of us that do have one. Partially because no normal human can feasibly think about only one thing all the time all their life (and Magnus <u><b>was</b></u> a normal human before his Awakening), partially because life is around you and you'll learning things either by exposition, curiosity or pressure. From the person that knows everything about anatomy because their siblings couldn't shut their mouths to the person that had to learn accounting because at the time they had to do people's taxes to make ends meet.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. To Magnus, magick is unbound potential. It is the rejection of absolute limits, the ability to look reality in the eye, and answer \u201cYou are wrong, and I will prove it\u201d when it tells you that something is impossible. That said, Magnus Magick is meant to be more instinctual and emotional and cerebral. He\u2019s not doing math equations or singing holy hymns.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I find it weird that he identifies his Magic as distinct from the other results of his training and life style. His Magic <i><b>is</b></i> his training, his lifestyle, his accomplishments.<br /> <br /> Overall a Mage thinking about their Magic as something they're morally bound to withhold is weird, and more likely sick than healthy.<br /> <br /> He may have actual reasons to not use Magic against some people, like not wanting to accidentally kill if he thinks this may happen, or thinking his better techniques are like sacred practices meant only for worthy challenges. But not because it's somehow more unfair than just being himself. Nothing is him more than his Magic.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8. These are more rote concepts than fully detailed ones, I still need to read up some more on the rules for spellcasting. They are mainly meant to focus around self-buffing stats, soak and healing, that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And still can be read as concepts and polished with the help of others.<br /> <br /> You don't have to share if you don't want to, but you can.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9. I\u2019m not entirely clear on how resonance levels work, I just read that you could give characters up to 3 points to start with, and Magnus is meant to be LOUD, both metaphysically and personally. I don\u2019t have any specific investment here, so I can tune that down.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, it isn't really something you want to mess with without knowing how the ST uses it.<br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind is that <i><b>everyone</b></i> is insanely driven in this game. Every Mage is just as dedicated and obsessed as Magnus, including the antagonists. Resonance 1 covers that already.<br /> <br /> The other, and even more important, is that high Resonance is the hallmark of a Mage with history, not a young, newly Awakened one. What increases your Resonance is your Magic and how you use it. It's the long time result of regularly building appropriate effects in significant situations.<br /> <br /> It is not a measure of personality. It's not a measure of presence. It's a measure of Magic, and how it's turning you into something <i>else</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus he is made to be a young, inexperienced mage, ideally paired with other similar mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game doesn't assume this assumption that a starting character is a new Mage. Nor that PCs will face simpler threats at first.<br /> <br /> While Mage is far from the hopelessness of other lines in the WoD, this is still the WoD. The system is highly lethal and the world is a dark, gritty place where secrecy and paranoia are the rules and stupidity can get you killed very fast.<br /> <br /> You <b>may</b> find a group where Magnus will work well. If the other players and ST all buy into it and the other PCs are willing to cover up Magnus' obvious liabilities, that can work, and even then this is a character running on borrowed time. But it can go royally wrong in a very unfun way. Keep that in mind if you really want to commit to a character that has no lifeline to minimally compensate their carelessness and ignorance (an <i>extremely</i> dangerous combination).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to start to try to metagame right off the bat, not that that'd be much fun regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not metagaming.<br /> <br /> Metagaming is when you take in-character decisions based on optimal game reward. This is about concept design and building to fit in a story.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms said, in the reality of gaming fitting with the group is more important than being strictly true to a concept, and &quot;that's my character&quot; won't fly as an excuse unless the group actually has fun with it.<br /> <br /> Which may happen, sure. But the defensive attitude is a problem, as even then people will notice if you're not easily willing to back down when you start to step on other's toes. Which will happen sooner or later because we're human.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556781#post1556781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as for the close combat aspect, he IS intended to use life magic to eventually move past the 5 maximum of stats (i am aware that will incur permadox or genetic flaws) i'm aware i can't just bulldoze him through everything, besides, what fun would that be?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll do very little for a long time.<br /> <br /> A costly buff to reach Strength 6, as he is now, will give him +1 Bashing damage when he succeeds in an attack to begin with. A kitchen knife will give him +1 or +2 damage depending on edition and increase category to Lethal, which means humans can't naturally soak to begin with (which includes Mages) and it may straight up kill you as soon as it fills the Health Boxes.<br /> <br /> While not the most extreme case, Storytelling is a highly lethal system and made to favor smart combat and compounding advantages. Increasing your capacity to cause harm through weapons and significant advantages is far easier than increasing your capacity to take it, and the baseline human is quite squishy.<br /> <br /> Magnus has just 7 Health boxes as everyone else, soaks an average of 2 damage from Bashing attacks alone, and has to get close to fight anyone just to deal 5 dice of Bashing damage. If you noticed, damage incurs penalties. They're heavy. A guy with a knife has a good chance of causing 2 unsoakable Lethal to Magnus in a single, simple attack, and things won't get better after that.<br /> <br /> That said... nothing of this is necessarily a problem, the problem is how overly committed he is to that. This game is not about combat, but precisely because of that yes, a character made <i>exclusively</i> for combat has to be superlative. Not because it'll make things easier, but because this is the <i>hardest</i> approach to almost every situation, so you have to be quite competent to pull it off reliably. And again, giving up on tools the game was built around isn't being fair, it's assuming a severe penalty. One your opponents won't assume.<br /> <br /> For whatever it's worth, by the way, at the end of the day wrestling is a sport. No one does it as a means to solve conflicts. It was never like that, and it existed farther back than writing. A Mage who really believes their wrestling is an effective tool in a fight should at least be actually very good at Magic through this Instrument instead of the player just relying on combat rules.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T05:16:43-08:00","id":1556833,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with being flexible if necessary, but that has to go in both directions. If the character is fundamentally unsuitable, okay, i'll have to come up with something else, but otherwise, if i adjust it to work the way other people want it to, then it's not my character anymore, it's a utility tool.<br /> <br /> As for combat effectiveness, given that you can use forces 2 to achieve impact forces over 8 times that of a shot from a glock 19 (i did the math) with simple redirection and concentration, the argument for shifting damage to lethal or even aggravated can easily be made. There's also nothing that stops Magnus from putting on armor, or using a ballistic shield, or smoke grenades, or anything else that helps keep him from getting shot.<br /> <br /> Also, the idea that wrestling is just a sport is just false. Many cultures and martial traditions have had a discipline of wrestling intended for combat. Just to give you an example from my own culture: Glima was designed specifically for fighting armed opponent as a means of unarmed self defense. In terms of pro wrestling, it's certainly made for theatrics, but if you don't hold back, don't use stunt choreography, and just straight up powerbombed someone, you could easily kill or catastrophically injure them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","user":"Ironguard","date":". 12-19-2025, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","name":"Ironguard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T14:27:44-08:00","id":1556844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556833#post1556833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with being flexible if necessary, but that has to go in both directions. If the character is fundamentally unsuitable, okay, i'll have to come up with something else, but otherwise, if i adjust it to work the way other people want it to, then it's not my character anymore, it's a utility tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is fundamentally a contradiction and not helping your case.<br /> <br /> You cannot be fine with being flexible for the sake of getting your character to mesh with the ST's idea for the game and the other players' desires, while claiming that adjusting your character to work more like what other people want ceases to make it &quot;your&quot; character.<br /> <br /> What's the point of even asking for our critiques? It's listening to us just going to turn Magnus from your character into a utility tool that we crafted?<br /> <br /> Given that you're responding in a fashion that feels defensive when we're trying to offer you advice for how to better actualize your character as well as things that we feel would be important considerations in how to tweak your character beyond that... there's a point where this gets to feeling futile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for combat effectiveness, given that you can use forces 2 to achieve impact forces over 8 times that of a shot from a glock 19 (i did the math) with simple redirection and concentration, the argument for shifting damage to lethal or even aggravated can easily be made. </div> </div> </div>Enough successes on a Forces 2 roll could justify lethal damage and increased damage dice. Sure, in theory, Forces 2 can let you punch for more damage than a normal firearm.<br /> <br /> 1) That's never going to be Aggravated damage. That's just not how the system works. If you want to do Agg as a mage, you need to infuse your attack with Prime, or use higher level effects. Life can deal Agg to living things when it gets to the point of being able to liquefy someone's insides (which is Life 3, so there's that). Forces starts doing Agg when you're disrupting the very energy that holds atoms together. Hitting things harder is just more damage dice. It also really doesn't matter that much. To the vast majority of things in the WoD filling all their Heath Boxes with damage + 1 more damage success is deadly regardless of Lethal or Aggravated tagged damage. Aggravated damage is just harder to soak and harder to heal (and healing only matters if it's not an insta-kill).<br /> <br /> 2) Where, exactly, is Magnus going to get all these successes? He doesn't have a Sanctum to do ritual magic in. He only gets 3 dice per roll. Etc. There's a big different between what is theoretically possible to do (get a ton of successes to increase the damage of an attack on Forces), and what your PC can realistic achieve with their current traits (he's lacking a lot of useful ones because they're not directly tied to hitting stuff).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also nothing that stops Magnus from putting on armor, or using a ballistic shield, or smoke grenades, or anything else that helps keep him from getting shot. </div> </div> </div>Not having a way to get any of those things is a hurdle that physical stats isn't going to overcome. Also he has Code of Honor, which you didn't fully spell out for us, but giving how you've talking about him not caring about such practical considerations and the Driven Flaw, I would assume he risks running afoul of said code if he starts to fight too &quot;dirty&quot; for his goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the idea that wrestling is just a sport is just false. </div> </div> </div>This is more of a semantic quibble. But &quot;wrestling&quot; is when combat grappling gets turned into a sport. Every martial tradition trains warriors/soldiers/etc. in unarmed combat and includes grappling in that training. But those are holistic unarmed systems in which grappling is one tool meant to be used in combination with the rest. When a combat tradition moves into the realm of just competing in grappling, we're outside of military combat and into sport.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just to give you an example from my own culture: Glima was designed specifically for fighting armed opponent as a means of unarmed self defense. </div> </div> </div>I... don't find that a very accurate summary of what's known about how glima originated. Like many parts of Norse/Nordic culture there's a significant gap that was created by the Viking era followed by the Christian conversions. But the evidence we do have indicates far more that glima followed the same path as most ancient combat systems: it was part of a holistic military training, that was formalized into competitive (aka sport) practices. We have hundreds of years of written evidence of glima competitions without people that specialize in glima for real combat. It's only much more recently that the highly formalized glima sport rules have been studied to recreate a more modern (though still far predates something like MMA or post-Napoleonic systematized military unarmed combat styles) unarmed self defense style that you can go train in today.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In terms of pro wrestling, it's certainly made for theatrics, but if you don't hold back, don't use stunt choreography, and just straight up powerbombed someone, you could easily kill or catastrophically injure them. </div> </div> </div>You can kill someone if you're not careful while racing cars. That doesn't make car racing an effective way of training for combat.<br /> <br /> Powerbombs are dangerous because they're flashy stunts where both athletes have to perform specific synchronized moves with no visible communication that the audience perceives to sell it as realistic. Powerbombs don't show up in combat manuals because they're dumb if your goal is to incapacitate your foes ASAP. To initiate a standard powerbomb, you already have to control your opponent's head and neck.... picking someone up to throw them when you can just directly attack the neck is not something you want people fighting for their lives to train to do.<br /> <br /> Pretty much the only time you're going to see a powerbomb that even remotely resembles a real fight is in MMA... and that's only because it's a functional retaliation to a failed triangle lock. The triangle lock skips the need to control your opponent so you can maneuver them into the position for the bomb, because they put themselves there already to obtain the lock. And people don't use triangle locks in life and death combat situations because at the most basic level they're submission holds, and submission holds are the last thing you want to do if your opponent has friends that might stumble onto your fight, or if your opponent can grab something long enough and pointy enough to shank you despite the reduced leverage the hold puts on unarmed counter attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T14:32:22-08:00","id":1556845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556833#post1556833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for combat effectiveness, given that you can use forces 2 to achieve impact forces over 8 times that of a shot from a glock 19 (i did the math) with simple redirection and concentration, the argument for shifting damage to lethal or even aggravated can easily be made.</div> </div> </div> </div>To Lethal, yes, that's a fact (but then your punch <b>may </b>be considered Vulgar. A gentle ST <b>may </b>grant that, since Magnus has so much evident Strength, it's still Concident to completely destroy someone with a punch). Aggravated , no, that's a different thing. It needs to be taking advantage of a supernatural weakness, Prime enhance the Force, or something like that - it's supernatural damage.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm a bit curious about that <b>math</b>: Forces can do, at Arete 3 assuming maximun successes (doable by stacking bonuses, but by no means granted) AND spending Willpower a grand total of 10 levels of damage (4 successes + 1 cuz Forces), more likely 8 (3 successes + 1). That's usually the <i>best </i>damage you can do on a single hit (the other option, lowering diffs. only it's better if you can stack a lot of bonuses from other sources - like using a really big weapon, have multiple actions, ambush. Etc.).<br /> <br /> A Glock has a damage of 4 + whatever you got on the attack roll (one of the reasons why Dex it's so massive), let's say you passed with 2 extra successes, and roll 6 dice (a dedicated gunner would roll a lot more, even w/o magick), that averages to 3 lethal. It's a lot less than 8-10. But not &quot;over 8 times less&quot;.<br /> <br /> Note that when you enhance an attack with magick, you have two options: Either you lower the difficulty of your <u>attack </u>roll, hit and solve the damage normally (and add +1 to the final damage if using Forces) OR you use the Damage Table. In that latter case <i>you don't roll to do extra damage</i> <i>nor add any extra </i>(incidentally, that means if you punch someone with Forces using DD your Strength it's kinda useless, Arete does all the damage and the muscles are just for show) <hr /><br /> EDIT: If it's as a Ritual, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Heavy Arms</a> pointed out, numbers make more sense. But then, even if we take the low estimate of you wanting to do 24 Lethal to get more than 8 times firing a Glock. That's 11 successes ... but let's say all we want it's <i>9</i> because 20 Lethal it's pretty close, and it's a LOT - and otherwise we go rigth into <i>Great Work</i> rules.<br /> <br /> This is Vulgar magick because not even <i>the Rock</i> can get away with punching like frigging rocket - so, difficulty 6, 5 if on the Node. One could argue for 7 base unless you want the punch to fail if sleepers are arround. One can lower further by spending resources, but Magnus doesn't have a lot of those.<br /> <br /> That's one Arete roll per hour, it's a <i>Ceremony</i> - let's say you expend one Willpower per roll to a maximum of 5 rolls (before entering into the even worse rules), that's 5 successes. Best possible scenario you need 4 more. But really, you need to account for 1s making you fail and increasing difficulties. At least Magnus won't botch (that's <i>very bad</i> on a ritual), but he <i>can </i>fail.<br /> <br /> All in all, If he sacrifices everything to it, I think Magnus <i>can </i>get away with this. Best case scenario, you've spended 3 to 5 hours to launch your <i>One Punch</i>...and it's <b><u>One</u></b> Punch.<br /> <br /> And w/o Time and w/o Prime, you have to either launch it immediately or &quot;save the last part of the ritual&quot;. And if you get interrupted midst a ritual (say, by getting injured before releasing your nuke), it's Willpower Difficulty 8, or blow up on Paradox as if you Boched. Neat.<br /> <br /> Yeah, mages can do a lot of damage, but this sort of ritual it's not exactly peak practicality. Not as a begginer with few resources at least. <hr /><br /> <br /> If you want to actually use your superior Strength in combat with Forces w/o it being just a glorified Paradox cushion, the word you're looking it's <b>Grapple</b> . That would allow you to attack with Strength instead of Dex, then you can inflict DD with Forces - and theres a lot of other fun stuff you could do using Forces to enhance a grapple, such as using the target as a human shield, or throwing him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also nothing that stops Magnus from putting on armor, or using a ballistic shield, or smoke grenades, or anything else that helps keep him from getting shot. </div> </div> </div>How is this more thematically appropiate than Magnus having a social circle?. Or otherwise having less exploitable weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> Armor isn't super great, even against mundane attacks, imagine against supernaturally powered ones. A Forces/Life effect casted as a ritual could help soack trully large amounts of some type of damage, like, Magnus could hold &quot;pure strength&quot; inside his muscles preventing cowardly guns from penetrating deep (a quick bus to Vulgar town if it's very strong, tho, and at ST discretion Unbelief could erode it).<br /> <br /> The main problem for a mage (and more so for Magnus) when Combat it's related isn't usually damage. It's action economy. Because Magnus doesn't care much about people, as he doesn't want to be saddled with them, he's going to get outnumbered every time. That means enemies get to act a lot, and you don't. It's *hard* for a mage to cope with this. Hence why acting first to get some sort of advantageous position would be very important. Too bad Magnus initiative ain't that great - we need to fix this (and the only <i>legal </i>way it's increasing Dexterity, as you can't increase Wits with that spread).<br /> <br /> And you really don't want to get ambushed - that's going to be trully awfull in terms of damage (they get to act before you, and the ambush roll gets added to the damage), and it's likely going to cause more damage than ordinary armor can soack, and, really, Magnus doesn't go everywhere in armor, does he?. And Magnus ain't great at not getting ambushed. Perhaps this should be your main focus on defensive magick rather than soack or damage. If you can act first, you can run away first, or use magick to turn the environment in your favor.<br /> <br /> A posibility using Life 2/Forces 1: &quot;instinctual defense&quot;. Magnus can instinctively recognize when an external power it's dangerous to his body and reacts automatically to protect itself like a surprised animal. Forces 1 detects the flow of forces on the vecinity, Life 1 can discriminate what forces are dangerous to your body, Life 2 can tie this sense into a reflex. That way maybe you could get to diminish the effectiveness of a surprise attack.<br /> <br /> If I could ask a house rule for this Rote, it would be getting to do the Dodge action within an Ambush, and if the ST it's ok with this, and you have an Instrument that can be used to Dodge, Violence as a Focus allows you to roll Arete while Dodging for a trully outrageous dodge that could also put you into an advantageous position. <hr /><br /> That is 3 rituals. Under M20 you can get away with it w/o penalties, in theory (in practice this may get overuled due to balance concerns). But even if you take in count all of this and get away scotch free, Magnus it's <i>still</i> not doing anything any other mage can't do, and he needs to be close to the enemies to do more.<br /> <br /> Does it mean it's <i>inviable</i>?. No, I don't think the <i>core</i> <i>concept </i>of a strongman brawler mage it's the problem - problem it's this idea of being also a trouble-seeker, that's <i>also </i>easily manipulable, that's <i>also </i>a sort of lone-wolf that doesn't care about other people.<br /> <br /> If he could be divorced from even one of these 3 extra weaknesses, it would be much more reasonable to get away with not being the best figther evah.<br /> <br /> For instance: A way to be more of a net positive as a character could be if he's willing to help others break trough their limits too (he has coaching Instruments after all). Instead of thinking only how to buff the character, let's think how to buff others (To buff others usually requires one Sphere dot higher, but if you can do it at all, it's a very resource-efficient way to use magick because it's only one extra success per extra target to get the full buff - it's a way to effectively <i>multiply </i>your power if you bestow this on trustworthy <i>allies </i>that would help you).<br /> <br /> The Cabal could benefit from that either participating on the training (and getting a &quot;free buff&quot; w/o needing to &quot;buff&quot; themselves), or by sending their Acolytes to train if they don't want to (even if they use guns, knowing hand-to-hand it's also important for a figther, and Magnus training it's <i>magickal</i>). In exchange, the Cabal can help him perform magick (sharing resources, maybe even participating if they can rationalize a way and have the Spheres). Being the chantry &quot;coach&quot; certainly sounds a more reasonable motive to have him arround than just being a bouncer that gets into too many figths. And he could do all of this at the same time he trains to improve himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-19-2025, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-20T01:54:37-08:00","id":1556851,"title":"","content":"HEAVY ARMS<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556844#post1556844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is fundamentally a contradiction and not helping your case.<br /> <br /> You cannot be fine with being flexible for the sake of getting your character to mesh with the ST's idea for the game and the other players' desires, while claiming that adjusting your character to work more like what other people want ceases to make it &quot;your&quot; character.<br /> <br /> What's the point of even asking for our critiques? It's listening to us just going to turn Magnus from your character into a utility tool that we crafted?<br /> <br /> Given that you're responding in a fashion that feels defensive when we're trying to offer you advice for how to better actualize your character as well as things that we feel would be important considerations in how to tweak your character beyond that... there's a point where this gets to feeling futile.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my perspective, you're being adversarial. There's a difference between offering critique (and preferably workable alternatives) and saying &quot;you should play the game the way i think is correct&quot; which is what this feels like. There's a difference between flexible adjustment and radical alteration.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556844#post1556844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Enough successes on a Forces 2 roll could justify lethal damage and increased damage dice. Sure, in theory, Forces 2 can let you punch for more damage than a normal firearm.<br /> <br /> 1) That's never going to be Aggravated damage. That's just not how the system works. If you want to do Agg as a mage, you need to infuse your attack with Prime, or use higher level effects. Life can deal Agg to living things when it gets to the point of being able to liquefy someone's insides (which is Life 3, so there's that). Forces starts doing Agg when you're disrupting the very energy that holds atoms together. Hitting things harder is just more damage dice. It also really doesn't matter that much. To the vast majority of things in the WoD filling all their Heath Boxes with damage + 1 more damage success is deadly regardless of Lethal or Aggravated tagged damage. Aggravated damage is just harder to soak and harder to heal (and healing only matters if it's not an insta-kill).<br /> <br /> 2) Where, exactly, is Magnus going to get all these successes? He doesn't have a Sanctum to do ritual magic in. He only gets 3 dice per roll. Etc. There's a big different between what is theoretically possible to do (get a ton of successes to increase the damage of an attack on Forces), and what your PC can realistic achieve with their current traits (he's lacking a lot of useful ones because they're not directly tied to hitting stuff).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Okay, let's get into the math i mentioned then, because what you just said doesn't make much sense to me.<br /> <br /> The formula for momentum is: p =mv<br /> <br /> A Glock 19 9mm handgun using a 124 grain bullet, has a projectile of about 8 gram or 0,008 kilogram, with an average muzzle velocity of 340-360 m/sec. If we presume close range and minimal loss of velocity before impact, let's put that at 350 m/sec.<br /> <br /> This gives us a p of 0,008 Kilograms (Masss) times 350 m/sec (velocity) = 2,8<br /> <br /> Now to translate that into kinetic energy, our formula is:<br /> <br /> KE = 0,5 x mv^2 (or 0,5 times mass, times velocity squared) which in this case gives us:<br /> <br /> 0,5 x 0,008 x (350 x 350) = 490 Joule<br /> <br /> Now sure, that doesn't sound like a lot, but when it comes to impact force, it becomes important. Given that impact force needs a stopping distance, lets select a fairly average for bullets of 0,5. This presume the bullet hits something hard, like bone, fairly quickly and imparts all its energy, as opposed to just passing through the target (which would waste a lot of the energy)<br /> <br /> the formula for kinetic impact is: F = KE / d (Force = Kinetic Energy / Distance) which gives us:<br /> <br /> 490 Joule / 0,005 meters = 98.000 Newtons (or 98 KiloNewtons)<br /> <br /> Now let's compare that to an elbow drop that uses Forces 2 to optimize kinetic flow in order to concentrate the impact of Magnus' full bodyweight onto an area the same size as a bullet. This isn't even a strike, this is just gravity doing work.<br /> <br /> Presuming a 3 meter drop (He's jumping off a table or a chair or some other slight elevation) and a standard gravity of 9,82 m/s per second acceleration, that gives us an impact speed of the following:<br /> <br /> Square root of 2gh (or 2 time gravity times height) which gives us an impact speed of 7,68 m/sec However, Magnus also has a weight of 140 Kilogram<br /> <br /> so plugging that into our previous formula, we now get:<br /> <br /> p = 140 x 7,68 = 1075 (rounded down)<br /> <br /> KE = 0,5 x 140 x (7,68 x 7,68) = 4128 J (rounded down)<br /> <br /> F = 4128 J / 0,005 m = 825,600 N or 825,6 Kn<br /> <br /> so to give proportion: 825,6 / 98 = 8,4 (rounded down) times the impact force of the bullet, fired at point blank range. Even if we just used the forces effect to shrink the impact area and not optimize Magnus' impact weight, he would still be AT LEAST as powerful as a bullet, and probably still substantially over that. We are already being extremely generous with the bullets circumstances.<br /> <br /> So what i am getting at here: using an extremely simple kinetic effect, Magnus' attack should be lethal damage. I'm not even asking for extra damage dice, which i easily could, i'm just arguing for conversion of damage type. If you want to say that i need to cast a ritual to do that, then there is no combat magic in this game. What are you going to cast in combat that's easier than simply shrinking impact area?<br /> <br /> With arete 3, willpower and using instruments, 2-3 successes should not be an unreasonable expectation. Are you saying i need more than that to cast a rote?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556844#post1556844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Also he has Code of Honor, which you didn't fully spell out for us, but giving how you've talking about him not caring about such practical considerations and the Driven Flaw, I would assume he risks running afoul of said code if he starts to fight too &quot;dirty&quot; for his goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Code of honor doesn't mean &quot;run naked and screaming towards gunfire&quot; it means you accept challenges, you accept surrender, you don't maliciously torment defeated enemies. In basic terms: Magnus is not a bully, and he doesn't like bullies. There's nothing dishonorable about putting on armor when you're fighting against opponents with weapons, especially if you're fighting barehanded, and there's nothing honorable about dying like a moron when your allies rely on you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556844#post1556844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> This is more of a semantic quibble. But &quot;wrestling&quot; is when combat grappling gets turned into a sport. Every martial tradition trains warriors/soldiers/etc. in unarmed combat and includes grappling in that training. But those are holistic unarmed systems in which grappling is one tool meant to be used in combination with the rest. When a combat tradition moves into the realm of just competing in grappling, we're outside of military combat and into sport.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> See this is exactly the kind of thing that makes it feel like you &quot;want to be right&quot; rather than &quot;want to help&quot; Like you said, it's a semantic quibble, and one mostly based on language. In my language, the word for &quot;wrestling&quot; and the word for &quot;grappling&quot; is the same.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> ALEPH<br /> <br /> I am aware that a lot of the effects i plan can be vulgar, but i'd rather eat a bit of paradox if it improves the chances of survival. Magnus is meant to be an attention sink for the enemy. He's there to give the rest of the cabal time to do their thing in peace. As for thematic propriety: If Magnus focus is combat, using combat tools to enable his fighting style seems entirely appropriate to me. Now as for the action economy, i mean that's really only applicable if the cabal actively sends him off on his own and just leaves him to die, in which case i would argue they are kind of being dicks.<br /> <br /> Also, i don't think ANYONE in the world of darkness react well to getting ambushed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In terms of defense, my primary idea was to use Life 3 to give him biokinetic armor that lets him soak lethal damage with his stamina pool. That should be a fairly simple rote, and if combined with things like kevlar should give him decent survivability as long as he's not getting hosed down by HMG fire.<br /> <br /> Also, i didn't say Magnus was a lone wolf who don't care about people. I said he's the kind of person that its difficult to maintain a long-term relationship with if you aren't actively in his sphere, which most people wouldn't be, because most people aren't active combat enthusiasts. A cabal of mages, who live in a much more dangerous world than ordinary people, would have a much better chance of maintaining a relationship, especially if Magnus has adopted himself as a sort of &quot;protector&quot; for them (which would be very in character for him)<br /> <br /> and focusing him around grappling is the point. He is a wrestler after all, not a boxer. The idea is to use grappling, clinches, throws, tackles, holds, etc. to disrupt and debilitate the enemy and buy time for everyone else to do their thing while Magnus soaks up the attention. Essentially, he's meant to be a melee focused control tank, not a bulldozer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","name":"Ironguard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-23T09:55:42-08:00","id":1556936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let's get into the math i mentioned then, because what you just said doesn't make much sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that math it's that Mage is nowhere near a physics simulator. There are very strict rules that regulate damage, much more strict than most Mage rules. We assumed you were using those somehow to get to that result.<br /> <br /> But, anyway. Yeah, converting the damage to Lethal it's entirely doable .<br /> <br /> I don't think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">monteparnas</a> was arguing against &quot;Magnus being able to do good damage&quot;, tho, as much as against the idea that raising Strength to 6 it's going to be a sizeable part of it. I would think of that stat as more of a &quot;statement&quot; (an act of Hubris that does make a ot of sense for Magnus) than the actual basis for combat<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, i don't think ANYONE in the world of darkness react well to getting ambushed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>And that's why it's so important<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In terms of defense, my primary idea was to use Life 3 to give him biokinetic armor that lets him soak lethal damage with his stamina pool. That should be a fairly simple rote, and if combined with things like kevlar should give him decent survivability as long as he's not getting hosed down by HMG fire. </div> </div> </div>It's a simple rote alrigth. Tho you would have to think about it in Maguns own terms (within his Focus). It's useful, but don't expect him to survive oponents that use magick on that basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now as for the action economy, i mean that's really only applicable if the cabal actively sends him off on his own and just leaves him to die, in which case i would argue they are kind of being dicks. </div> </div> </div>Unlike D&amp;D, on WoD games it's very common for characters to be on their own. As each has distinct interests. It's almost 100% likely your Cabal mates aren't going to follow (or care about) Magnus career as an underground figther. He's going to be alone and figthing a lot of times. And the &quot;underground&quot; doesn't suggest people who would play fairly at all.<br /> <br /> OFC no good person it's going to send Magnus alone against a powerful, <i>and common</i>, enemy. but that assumes the cabal even knows this is happening. Magnus it's going to get a lot of enemies of his own due to how he acts, and it's extremely unlikely they aren't going to target Magnus when he's alone.<br /> <br /> Having some basic prep, like soacking lethal, it's going to be OK for mundane enemies that heavily underestimate what Magnus can do, but expecting to survive there if the ST it's planning a serious confrontation of any kind can use a bit more of tactical thinking, and actually using the resources Mage has to provide rather than ignoring them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, i didn't say Magnus was a lone wolf who don't care about people. I said he's the kind of person that its difficult to maintain a long-term relationship with if you aren't actively in his sphere, which most people wouldn't be, because most people aren't active combat enthusiasts. </div> </div> </div>Most people on the &quot;underground combat&quot; sphere are definitely going to be human, and a lot of them, probably most of them, are going to be combat enthusiasts. Even those that don't know how to figth are going to &quot;be there&quot; cheering, working, making shady deals, and Magnus it's going to want to talk to them because he likes to talk to people. And if he's <i>likeable</i>, then people it's going to like him back. Then he can, potentially, get to know dependable people (even if he himself can't distinguish flattery from genuine interest).<br /> <br /> I don't see the problem unless he's trully more trouble than he's worth - and you said he ain't going to bring trouble on purpose. But he isn't good at identifying trouble, so he should either become good at it, or know someone that can help doing that<br /> <br /> Incidentally, a good way to face ambushes is to know about them beforehand. Those 3 &quot;shotgun thugs&quot; aren't going to be so scary if you appear breaking the wall besides them, rather than looking confused on the line of fire as they expected. Thus havings some way to keep tabls on the underground would help you survive there w/o much help from the Cabal<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A cabal of mages, who live in a much more dangerous world than ordinary people, would have a much better chance of maintaining a relationship </div> </div> </div>I don't see that so clearly. Mages live on the same world as normal people. There's not a ViP Underground where only mages get to access (or, well, there may be one - but it would be far from the norm).<br /> <br /> Mages are extremely good at working with normal people, as long as those people share their belief. They both reinforce the mage's magick and can be reinforced by it. Hence why normal Chantries include large amounts of normal people that work with the mages and face the same danger.<br /> <br /> And, believe it or not, Mages sometimes try to solve stuff w/o combat. There's alot of creative stuff to do that doesn't involve getting into a figth. But even when they do go to War, Mages often fight by proxy - deliberately avoiding direct conflict.<br /> <br /> Mages are extremely good sharing their power, hiding, and managing distances. Mages are at their weakest when they face an unexpected enemy. Put 2 and 2 together: this kind of mages aren't going to want a <i>colleague </i>soacking up attention anywhere near them. Because that role on such a game can be described with another word: &quot;decoy&quot; ... But they can't do that to a fellow, now, can they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if Magnus has adopted himself as a sort of &quot;protector&quot; for them (which would be very in character for him) </div> </div> </div>Except Magnus isn't really THAT good at it, and you're banking on the Cabal protecting Magnus a lot.<br /> <br /> So, optimally, the rest of the cabal are going to be the ones doing all the political stuff that's needed to survive on WoD, seeking intel to avoid ambushes and other problems, planning the figths, and they would also have to pull Magnus out of the troubles he seeks for himself (solving the legal or social issues he's bound to face as part of the underground that's easily manipulable and doesn't know even his basic rigths, be sure he's not outnumbered by the personal enemies he's bound to make, and such ... or be accused of leaving him &quot;on his own&quot;).<br /> <br /> Or, in other words, you're banking on <i>them </i>to be your &quot;Allies Background&quot;. And if they do play along, then there's no problem. The concern here it's, what if they don't want to play along?.<br /> <br /> If the Cabal wants to avoid combat, Magnus would be left all alone a lot of the time. If they want to hide and figth from the shadows, Magnus it's going to either be a burden or a decoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-23-2025, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-27T03:59:03-08:00","id":1557040,"title":"","content":"I suppose i should specify a bit how i intended for Magnus to work in relation to stealth, or group combat. Like i mentioned, he's meant to act as an attention sink for the enemy, so if the party will want a more stealthy approach, using Magnus as a distraction is entirely within what i intended, and what he's good for. In combat specifically, he's meant to survive the enemy's attention long enough to get into close combat, at which point he'll shift from simply absorbing, to debilitating, mainly through grapples. Let me lay out what i got so far in terms of basic loadout, because i don't think saying Magnus can't protect the party is entirely fair. I'll go over this in quick, functional terms rather than the whole narrative and thematic for each rote.<br /> <br /> Equipment:<br /> Kevlar - Relatively easy to obtain, and there's no shame in armor when facing guns. I believe the standard is 3 soak against bullets?<br /> Ballistic shield - Also relatively easy to obtain or improvise. Extra soak would be nice, but ideally it will work like directional cover. This is meant to be used on approach and easily discarded upon entering melee, as to not hamper grappling.<br /> Smoke grenades (Optional) - not necessarily a commercial smoke grenade, something as simple as a homemade flour bomb could serve a similar purpose. Meant to briefly obscure vision while closing to melee.<br /> <br /> Magic:<br /> Biokinetic armor (Life 3) - Allows magnus to soak incoming lethal using his stamina pool.<br /> Stamina buff (Life 3) - Increases stamina, improves soak when combined with Biokinetic armor<br /> Kinetic Dispersion (Forces 2) - Disperses energy from hits across Magnus entire body. Ideally is meant to lower soak difficulty, though a flat damage reduction for a set number of hits could work too)<br /> Adrenaline burst - Allows Magnus to ignore wound penalties for the duration of the scene. Must test willpower for fatigue afterwards<br /> Synaptic overdrive - Provides a bonus to initiative. Must test willpower for fatigue afterwards.<br /> <br /> Now, a few of these will be vulgar depending on circumstance, and probably if used all together. Ideally, they'll be used selectively depending on the needs of the fight, or as pre-fight buffs if Magnus knows he's going into combat. I suspect i might want a ritual to combine all the effects into basically a &quot;war mode&quot; style buff. However, with just some of these on, Magnus should be able to withstand gunfire from multiple shooters for at least a couple of rounds, and still be healthy enough to make it into melee, unless he's quite unlucky.<br /> <br /> This IS all geared towards mundane-equivalent opponents with guns. Hopefully the ST isn't going to throw Fomori bruisers at us right off the bat. Plus once Magnus does get into melee range, his high strength should give him an advantage when grappling, which will give him options to disrupt enemies. In a party situation, that also means the other members have more time and freedom to do their actions while the enemy is shooting at Magnus. If you have any suggestions for refinements/additions, i am all ears.<br /> <br /> Now in a solo scenario, this is all going to depend a lot on the number of opponents. Mind you, Magnus wants challenge, not suicide. He's smart enough to run away if he's going up against 4 people with assault rifles on his own. That's not cowardice, it's not being a moron.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;avoid combat&quot; front though, i am considering just dropping the Brawl 5 idea entirely and moving some points into intimidate. Even if he's not malicious, an argument can be made that Magnus sheer physicality might dissuade people from wanting to tangle with him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","name":"Ironguard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-28T03:13:27-08:00","id":1557053,"title":"","content":",Looking at your responses, some misunderstandings I got earlier became more clear.<br /> <br /> The main issue, and that's something very clear for those with experience on both games, is that you're looking at it with D&amp;D lenses. You're fundamentally thinking through the &quot;dungeon crawling mindset&quot;, where the story happens outside normal life and the PCs are explorers deliberately (even if unwillingly) exploring dangerous areas or situations that are not the &quot;mundane reality&quot; of normal people.<br /> <br /> WoD doesn't work like that, for <i>several</i> reasons. Typical chronicles are about dangers lurking <i>within daily life</i>, when characters are going through their routines or at least walking in perfectly normal, civilized areas. You're not ambushed exploring the woods, you're ambushed going to the grocery store. You live among normal people, doing normal things, and so do your enemies, and everything in this world that's dangerous and/or malicious is hiding in plain sight all the time. Trouble just doesn't happen in distinct, identifiable, manageable contexts.<br /> <br /> It isn't a game with clear challenges and victory conditions, either. It's not that you have other tools than combat to solve problems, it's that most problems aren't about combat at all, and even to solve them through violence requires some lateral thinking. How do you beat your way through an eviction notice? What do you do when the enemy's lair (and I mean it, it may well be a lair) is in a corporate building with top security and legal clout? What do you do when your enemy can be anyone in the streets? Or when they simply know where you live and your routine and can stage an attack for any point in the future? Those aren't just things that happen in WoD, they're <i>the regular state of the game</i>.<br /> <br /> Finally, <b>dealing with consequences is half the fun</b>. In WoD your actions happen almost all the time within the bounds of a society with roles and expectations. You have to worry about evidence, witnesses, the police, innocent bystanders, collateral damage, the law, what your neighbors will think, all the time, and the supernatural society isn't a substitute for this, it's a layer <i>on top</i> of that. The bulk of the game is about navigating this environment while doing supernatural shit, and dealing with the consequences of failing, by accident or choice.<br /> <br /> Our advice comes from this whole difference in game dynamics. In WoD your behavior outside combat matters a lot, and you can be a liability for others and yourself way before any brawl starts. There is no clear distinction between when we're in the adventure and when we're not, never. Blurring the lines is the very point, and you can't treat fight situations as fundamentally distinct from just living your life. The story almost always happen during your daily life.<br /> <br /> Now, there is some more pointy critique to be made, here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1556851#post1556851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my perspective, you're being adversarial. There's a difference between offering critique (and preferably workable alternatives) and saying &quot;you should play the game the way i think is correct&quot; which is what this feels like. There's a difference between flexible adjustment and radical alteration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms has a direct and sometimes rude way of saying things, but it has been far from that.<br /> <br /> Literally no one here tried to change your character, but to help you implement your concept while making something better adapted to the reality of the game we have actual experience with. And if many changes were pointed, it's because you have many options, not because anyone demanded you implement everything.<br /> <br /> But you <b>have</b> been consistently defensive and resistant to change, with few very minor exceptions that help, but do not really address the main problems. You don't engage almost anything we say for real, just justify why you think we're wrong and your character needs no change.<br /> <br /> The others explained well my points on wrestling and strength. You can do a lot of damage <i><b>with your Magic</b></i> all right, but that has nothing to do with your combat build. And not only does Magic carries it's own considerations, it isn't an exclusive thing. 99,99% of the population can't do nothing about it, sure, but 99,99% of the population won't be your real problem at any given time. And for that matter, even with Magic defensive effects scale far, far less than offensive ones. And your Strength score won't matter much for your Magic, nor will getting from 5 to 6 be a game-changing combat feat.<br /> <br /> Unarmed fighting has a well defined and much deserved place in military training and self defense, but <b><u>dedicated unarmed combat</u></b> isn't a combat strategy. It's an important foundation for armed combat, and an important skill for edge cases (which is what self-defense is about), but trying to solve actual problems by fighting unarmed is just not how it has ever worked. That's why while being an important foundation, it has always been depicted and recorded in every place, by every culture, as either training, sports, edge cases or feats for legendary heroes (who don't need to do logic). Glima is no exception to this.<br /> <br /> Grappling, for whatever it matters, work in self defense because in those situations you're frequently at close quarters with someone who's threatening to harm you, but are not actively doing so yet. Even then any self-defense instructor worth their salt will tell you that the most important things in self-defense are alertness and avoidance, and the best strategy in a confrontation with an armed assailant is to comply and de-escalate, because no matter how good you are, your chances aren't that great. And for every story of a fighter that got away from assault by beating their assailant, there are two or three of fighters who got seriously injured or killed trying.<br /> <br /> More important, though, is how the game systems work it, and WoD is simply a very lethal game where weapons make a lot of difference, as do any extraneous advantage. Numbers and initiative easily decide the outcome, any damage is a heavy hindrance, and no source of harm can be safely dismissed even by the most powerful characters. The idea is to use your resources to have the greatest advantage you can get and treat combat as a scary prospect that can easily go wrong if you don't <b>take</b> control of the situation.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1557040#post1557040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This IS all geared towards mundane-equivalent opponents with guns. Hopefully the ST isn't going to throw Fomori bruisers at us right off the bat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is totally a thing in WoD.<br /> <br /> As it isn't an exploration, enemies aren't silo'ed in predictable points, and as numbers and plans matter a lot and combat isn't a default solution, confronting the PCs with far superior foes isn't at all uncommon. Picking up a fight with something way above your weight category without noticing is a constant risk, and even those way below can cause a lot of trouble if they get advantages like surprise, numbers and/or good weapons (2 out of 3 is plenty here).<br /> <br /> Party situations are far less than a thing in WoD. Unless the group is ostensibly a paramilitary unit, they're unlikely to work as one in any regular basis. It's less that they won't want to help and more that they won't be good at that. Magnus is a fitting bruiser/tank (at least conceptually) for a combat party where everyone has a combat role, but that's rarely a thing in Mage. You're more likely to be paired with a lawyer, a street artist and an old recluse with Parkinson. Characters tailor made for combat either exist within a cabal tailor made for combat or, more commonly, have means to make combat go their way without the cabal, and the wits to actively avoid combat (frequently their main role in a group is to detect and avoid problems instead of fighting it).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately another trait of the system is that it's even more random than D&amp;D when it comes to dice rolling. Harmless head-shots and lethal umbrella thrusts are things that happen with just enough frequency to be a known quantity. You shouldn't rely on average results.<br /> <br /> I did had a Magnus-style PC in my Mage game until recently (the player had to leave the game) as I said before, but this player talked to the group beforehand about the character and was totally aware that he would be a liability, <i>it was the point</i>, he wanted to be a comic relief that causes (minor and funny) problems with his trouble-seeking attitude instead of solving them with combat. It worked because everyone was on board, and the player knew his actual contributions would rarely be through combat (the other PCs were a financial advisor who was frequently throwing money at problems, a sword-aficionado youtuber that didn't expect to use the sword, either, and two retired elders, one of whom dotted on the boxer as a grandchild).<br /> <br /> Not saying that Magnus has to be a comic-relief or anything, but an example of how the game do not rely on some of his current assumptions.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T14:24:04-08:00","id":1557103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1557040#post1557040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like i mentioned, he's meant to act as an attention sink for the enemy, so if the party will want a more stealthy approach, using Magnus as a distraction is entirely within what i intended, and what he's good for.</div> </div> </div> </div>How, exactly, is he good for this? He lacks the social stats to do anything more than put on the air of a menacing brute. As monteparnas has stated in detail, this is a game set in the modern world that at least on the surface works like it. If Magnus comes up to the front of a secured facility dressed for a fight? The guards are going to put the facility on lockdown (making his teammates' lives harder), leave him to wrestling with a steel security door with his bare hands, and take up firing positions that he can't just walk up to due to cover or height advantages. They're also just going to call the cops like normal sane people would (assuming dozens of people haven't already because a huge guy in body armor and carrying a ballistic shield is walking around with grenades hanging on his vest).<br /> <br /> What does that accomplish for the goal of stealth and whatever investigation/etc. the other PCs wanted to do? Is Magnus going to fight the cops too, or just get arrested and face years of prison time (I'm not aware of any country that's cool with people that build IEDs, even ones meant to be less-than-lethal, and then try to pick fights against normal citizens while carrying said devices; wearing body armor tends to make it worse for your legal troubles as well).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In combat specifically, he's meant to survive the enemy's attention long enough to get into close combat, at which point he'll shift from simply absorbing, to debilitating, mainly through grapples. </div> </div> </div>And he gets into close combat and then dies pretty much instantly anyway. Magnus is, as currently written, built for one-on-one fights. That's the only thing he can manage.<br /> <br /> If you're fighting multiple opponents in close-combat, you take +1 difficulty on your attack and defense rolls per opponent. So, two opponents? +2 difficulty on your attacks, including your grapples, because it's hard to keep your holds with someone else is actively attacking you to help their friend get free. Since you're grappling you can't do anything to stop opponents from circling around to get a flanking bonus, guns get a bonus in close combat, and attacking someone in a grapple also gets a bonus since they can't move around freely.... leaving all those unrestrained opponents with the freedom to take a high end targeted shot to avoid your armor, get +2 damage dice on top of all that, and still be rolling at minimum attack difficulty. Swapping Matter 1 for Mind 1 would help a lot here since you didn't put Matter into any of your proposed effects, and Mind 1 can among many things eliminate the penalties on your rolls for being outnumbered.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, the armor is a -1 dice penalty to all your Dex based rolls, and a ballistic shield is another -1 penalty there, so any Dex based rolls you don't have Ability dots in as well are autofails until you drop the shield, and that -2 is also going to suck for your Dex + Athletics rolls to get to any opponents that aren't standing in easy places for you to attack them. This is a huge problem since the best bonuses from a shield require an active Dex + Melee roll... and you have no Melee dots. Even if you swapped to Dex 3, you'd be rolling 1 die at +1 diff meaning that shield is not going to be all that useful against guns (though you could move at half speed and double the turns of them freely shooting at you if you'd like some Cover).<br /> <br /> When I said you have picked the least mechanically effective way of doing combat in this game, I was not being hyperbolic. You don't need to be worried about fomori. You need to be worried that your ST doesn't just fiat that Magnus takes a bullet to the head, goes into a coma, and then is in the hospital under police supervision so that the group can rescue him before he's removed from the game because he can't do anything from prison for a few years.<br /> <br /> Yes, even in combat, even with all that gear and magic, he's a liability, not a powerhouse. If he's lucky to keep normal human guards busy for 30 seconds before they incapacitate him and he'll maybe injure one of them, how is he supposed to protect other people?<br /> <br /> I'm also going to put out again that Magnus lacks key dots for what you're saying. Kevlar vest and a ballistic shield? Not hard to get but not cheap, especially for a character that can't buy stuff off the rack and needs custom built gear for his size. He's only got Resources 2. Modern ballistic counter measures are not designed to be repaired easily, they're designed to be replaced. It's not ~$750 US (not including shipping or tax) for a quality Kevlar vest w/trauma plates that's made to fit him, it's that price after every fight he has to soak lethal or agg damage because you can't fix Kevlar without magic. Once the weave is compromised, you need to replace it. A homemade shield is going to be the same thing, buying one is going to be much more expensive (though they're more durable).<br /> <br /> Also... he's got no Crafts, no Technology, and no Science... how is he making a shield or building smoke grenades? He doesn't have any Backgrounds related to people that could get him these things. Where are they coming from? His zero dots in Streetwise ability to find black market dealers and not get ripped off?<br /> <br /> Sure, for a mage that knows what they're doing this is trivial. Magnus doesn't know this stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kinetic Dispersion (Forces 2) - Disperses energy from hits across Magnus entire body. Ideally is meant to lower soak difficulty, though a flat damage reduction for a set number of hits could work too) </div> </div> </div>This is going to be a very ST dependent rote and I wouldn't rely on it being allowed. Messing with damage/soak difficulties via supernatural powers is a very rare effect.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Forces 2 in particularly tends to be a two-way street in its effects. If you bend light around yourself to turn invisible, you also can't see without magic to extend your senses beyond your stealth field. If you alter how a character interacts with kinetic energy it's going to matter both ways as well. Strikes against him would disperse across a wider surface area, but his own attacks would be equally weakened as he can't concentrate impacts on small areas of his body either. Not necessarily a bad thing if you want to grapple and immobilize without damage, but that's not really a winning tactic in a fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Adrenaline burst - Allows Magnus to ignore wound penalties for the duration of the scene. Must test willpower for fatigue afterwards<br /> Synaptic overdrive - Provides a bonus to initiative. Must test willpower for fatigue afterwards. </div> </div> </div>All the more reason to grab Mind 1 over trying to do this with Life 2 or 3.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> More broadly on the magic side of things:<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that you take difficulty increases as you stack on more and more effects. Loading up on lots of prep effects makes casting on-the-fly very hard to do, and can even make the last few effects you try unreliable. Reliably having 3+ effects running is always going to be better as ritual magic cast in advance with extra successes put towards duration.<br /> <br /> Magnus has a lot of Willpower, but Willpower points recover relatively slowly. Even with that 9 rating, with this much magic you can't reliably spend WP on every roll, and then you're risking having zero to spend in the actual scene.<br /> <br /> Trying to combine things into a single big effect has a bunch of drawbacks (increased number of successes, rolling at the higher difficulty for some effects that could be easier if cast solo, still being a WP sink), and you have to explain it all in a fashion that matches your Focus to your ST's satisfaction. Once you're facing supernatural opponents this also gets into a severely disadvantageous position of losing all your buffs to a single counterspell.<br /> <br /> You haven't even included any offensive magic in this. Or social boosting magic that could keep enemies aggro on you instead of doing things like triggering a silent alarm. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not cowardice, it's not being a moron. </div> </div> </div>That is still up in the air for Magnus. The Code of Honor Merit is one you have to personalize and detail. The Merit is vague not because you just have to act exceptionally honorably by some unspecified standard, but because you have to specify a standard that is above and beyond the norms for both your Sleeper social norms and any norms of your magical associations. Don't expect a ST to let you have the Merit if Magnus doesn't have things he'll be willing to die for rather than compromise on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T06:00:26-08:00","id":1557146,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28996\" data-vbnamecard=\"28996\">Ironguard</a> From someone who has experienced this in this forum, do not take what people say here too harshly.<br /> <br /> Your character ia great and it seems to fit well what you are looking for in the game. Remember, this is just a fucking game and everyone should just have fun. Things like wrestlers bodyfat doesn't fucking matters, you can have your bodybuilder/fighter/weight lifter at 5% bf and that's ok, it's not real life it's a game.<br /> <br /> You can also have the char you want without worrying exactly how you would add to the group, imho, that's something that the ST would have to work out.<br /> <br /> Now, what *I* would do is maybe rearrange some stats. Probably shift 1 from str to dex, but it's ok if you don't want it. Having str already at 5 means you wont use magick to increase it, unless you want to deal with pattern bleeding.<br /> <br /> Also, something that I find *very* odd in the setting is that notion that if you dont have a dot in a stat you are completely clueless of it. Like the academics and computer thing. I believe a great majority of the population made at least to high-school and knows how to operate the basic of a computer, so this means every char needs to spend dots on those? I'm not sure about that.<br /> <br /> Well, having said all that, I wouldn't necessarily change anything in this char, just have fun with it. And one last thing, I would love to see those rotes, because it seems he is too limiting, imho, with the focus you provided. It seems he can only get some combat buffs and that's it\u2026 Forces is an incredible sphere and all you seem to use it for is to give him some combat buffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 12-30-2025, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T10:46:18-08:00","id":1557149,"title":"","content":"First off, i want to apologize if it seems like i've skipped over some things. December has been stressful to say the least, and i haven't been at my best focus. I've mostly focused on what seemed to be the greater points of friction at the time. That said, i do appreciate all the feedback, and will take it under due consideration. I hope you all have a great new year ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard","name":"Ironguard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T11:36:55-08:00","id":1557152,"title":"","content":"I agree with all the posts above, and can't really add much anything.<br /> <br /> Except this part:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can also have the char you want without worrying exactly how you would add to the group, imho, that's something that the ST would have to work out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not just dump this resposability entirely on the STs shoulder. ST has a lot of work already, and also wants to have fun.<br /> <br /> The players should help the ST with this, talk to each other and decide their own dynamics.<br /> <br /> Having a &quot;session 0&quot; to present the character it's a great idea always on almost any game, and it's going to be more informative about what things to change about Magnus, if any, than anything we could theorize.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T08:52:11-08:00","id":1557259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1557152#post1557152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with all the posts above, and can't really add much anything.<br /> <br /> Except this part:<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's not just dump this resposability entirely on the STs shoulder. ST has a lot of work already, and also wants to have fun.<br /> <br /> The players should help the ST with this, talk to each other and decide their own dynamics.<br /> <br /> Having a &quot;session 0&quot; to present the character it's a great idea always on almost any game, and it's going to be more informative about what things to change about Magnus, if any, than anything we could theorize.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, a session 0 is always good, and the ST also should have fun. My point is that he shouldn't build his char thinking worrying that he wont be useful for stealth and he wont be useful for this or that. Just make the char you want and work his backstory with the ST. People here are judging the char too much imo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T19:30:25-08:00","id":1557295,"title":"","content":"Revan... it's a critique thread... the whole point is to judge the character. Ideally we also try to add more input than that and all, but that's the central premise of asking others to critique your work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T03:12:47-08:00","id":1557302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1557146#post1557146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28996-ironguard\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28996\" data-vbnamecard=\"28996\">Ironguard</a><br /> You can also have the char you want without worrying exactly how you would add to the group, imho, that's something that the ST would have to work out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree, as an ST I really like when players take the initiative to at least worry about how their characters will work within the group.<br /> <br /> Talking like that you put the whole pressure upon the ST's shoulders. And this may be ok within groups that already have a healthy dynamic to begin with, so this has never been a problem, but this is not everyone's reality, much less when you're looking for a new group to play with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1556668-m20-first-character-critique-request?p=1557259#post1557259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that he shouldn't build his char thinking worrying that he wont be useful for stealth and he wont be useful for this or that. Just make the char you want and work his backstory with the ST. People here are judging the char too much imo</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside the fact that's exactly what was asked for, I'll restate that you should definitely worry at least a little about how your character can work properly if you want to find a new group, because by default you have no idea how those people, especially the ST, work.<br /> <br /> Here we also have a lot of questions about expectations of the very player who'll play the character. It's extremely common for new players, even those who devoured the books, to expect things to work one way, and find during play they simply don't. More than making Magnus an effective what-have-you, we're trying to help the build match the concept and expected play experience. That has a lot to do with identifying what the player thinks will happen and what will likely happen, and suggest ways to bridge the gaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}